  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Find the center and radius of the circle whose equation is ${x}^{2}-10x+{y}^{2}+4y+25=0.$",
  "worked_solution": "To find the center and radius of the circle, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-10x+{y}^{2}+4y+25 & =0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-10x)+({y}^{2}+4y) & =-25 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 5x+{5}^{2})+({y}^{2}+2\\cdot 2y+{2}^{2}) & =-25+{5}^{2}+{2}^{2} \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 5x+25)+({y}^{2}+2\\cdot 2y+4) & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can factor the perfect squares and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-5)^{2}+(y+2)^{2} & =4 \\\\ (x-5)^{2}+(y-(-2))^{2} & ={2}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(5,-2)$ and its radius is $2.$",
